      "problem": "Calculate $\\left(\\dfrac{2x}{3}\\right)^4.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2x}{3})}^{4}=\\frac{(2x)^{4}}{{3}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2x)^{4}}{{3}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{4}{x}^{4}}{{3}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{16{x}^{4}}{81} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
